   "id": "spcpt_JHTSXV648T9G7tDK",
   "name": "Wave & tide power",
   "definition": null,
   "video_id": "856127744"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Wave & tide power"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Energy can be obtained from the kinetic store of the waves and tides\n- The motion of the water is used to turn a turbine, which turns a generator, which generates electricity"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Wave power"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Wave power uses underwater turbines\n- The waves move the water which causes the turbines to turn"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Turbines using wave power"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2022/08/1-8-3-tidal-power-cie-igcse-23-rn.png",
   "file": "assets/30822d4c2ca7-1-8-3-tidal-power-cie-igcse-23-rn.png",
   "alt": "1-8-3-tidal-power-cie-igcse-23-rn",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***Underwater turbines generate electricity***"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Tidal power"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Tidal power uses tidal barrages to store water at a height as the tide comes in and goes out\n- When the barrage is opened, water flows through a channel over a turbine"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Tidal barrage"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2023/03/1-8-3-a-tidal-barrage-produces-elelctricity-using-tides-cie-igcse-rn-colour-1.png",
   "file": "assets/bf4a4a25005e-1-8-3-a-tidal-barrage-produces-elelctricity-usin.png",
   "alt": "1-8-3-a-tidal-barrage-produces-elelctricity-using-tides-cie-igcse-rn-colour-1",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***A tidal barrage stores water at a height and then opens a gate allowing water to flow over a turbine***"
  },
  {
   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_jHPjKGJzsd2v7tdx",
   "name": "Hydroelectric dams",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Hydroelectric dams"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- When water is stored above ground level, it has energy in its **gravitational potential store**\n- This energy can be transferred to **kinetic energy** if the water is allowed to flow down the slope\n- Flowing water turns the turbine to **generate electricity**"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "A hydroelectric dam"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2022/08/1-8-3-hydroelectric-dam-cie-igcse-23-rn.png",
   "file": "assets/04a0d55e5e62-1-8-3-hydroelectric-dam-cie-igcse-23-rn.png",
   "alt": "1-8-3-hydroelectric-dam-cie-igcse-23-rn",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***A hydroelectric dam transfers energy mechanically from the gravitational potential energy store of the water to its kinetic energy store. The moving water turns the turbine***"
  }
